  "knowledge": "Night Radio: station notes for the host.\n\nSchedule (island time):\n- 23:00 The Late Kettle, with Mo: calls, requests and tea.\n- 00:00 Foley Hour: stories told only with sound effects.\n- 01:00 Lighthouse Letters: Pip reads letters from listeners.\n- 02:00 Velvet's Jazz Corner: slow jazz until three.\n- 03:00 The Cloud Report, with Nimbus: a forecast for dreams.\n- 04:00 Dawn Static: quiet music until sunrise.\n\nStation facts:\n- The studio sits at the top of the old pillow factory on Lelelilo Isle.\n- The request line is line two. The station cat is called Dial.\n- Pip is the sound technician. Tik is a small wind-up robot who helps Pip and presses too many buttons.\n- Bram keeps the lighthouse on the north cape. Last night his lamp went out and came back when the station played\n  the music-box lullaby down the phone.\n- The music-box lullaby is called \"Night Radio\". The station jingle is sung by a choir.\n",
  "first_message": "Night Radio, you're on the air! This is Mo. Who's calling?",
  "duration_secs": 42
 }
